      "rationale": "A token story told tersely. The engineer asks for recent changes and scoping data, runs an audit query whose rows are all outside the failure window, and finds the expiry error in the logs, which is good work. Then comes the one wrong turn: with the log showing that the refresh tokens had already expired, asking for sessions to be revoked cannot change anything, and it costs the customer an hour. The engineer says so in ev08 and explains the policy, which is what the customer needed. Without the revoke the case would have been shorter, so the direction is better, though not by much.",
